        "2025-02-28"^^xsd:date,
        "2025-03-04"^^xsd:date ;
    dcterms:relation onto:etcsLevelType,
        onto:gprsForETCS ;
    dcterms:source <http://data.europa.eu/eli/reg_impl/2023/1695/oj> ;
    rdfs:comment "Indication of the area in which GPRS can be used for ETCS, expressed as a list of GPRS-enabled RBCs."@en ;
    rdfs:domain [ a owl:Class ;
            owl:unionOf [ a rdf:List ;
                    rdf:first onto:CommonCharacteristicsSubset ;
                    rdf:rest [ a rdf:List ;
                            rdf:first onto:RunningTrack ;
                            rdf:rest () ] ] ] ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy onto: ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string ;
    rdfs:seeAlso "Sections of EIRENE optional for trackside in TSI"@en ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf onto:tsiCompliantRadioDataParameter ;
    ns1:term_status "stable" ;
    skos:scopeNote "Since GPRS can be used for ETCS, indicate in which areas it is implemented (e.g.: whole section, only between two signals, at the station…)"@en .

onto:gradient a owl:DatatypeProperty,
        owl:FunctionalProperty ;
    rdfs:label "Gradient for stabling tracks"@en ;
    onto:XMLName "ILL_Gradient" ;
    onto:applicable "Y/N" ;
    onto:legalDeadline "In accordance with Implementing Decision 2014/880/EU and by 16 March 2019 at the latest"@en ;
    onto:rinfIndex "1.2.2.0.3.1" ;
    onto:shaclShapeValidationRule <http://data.europa.eu/949/shapes/Gradient> ;
    onto:unitOfMeasure <http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MilliM-PER-M> ;
    onto:usedInRCCCalculations true ;
    dcterms:created "2021-08-10"^^xsd:date ;
    dcterms:modified "2021-08-10"^^xsd:date,
        "2024-09-19"^^xsd:date,
        "2025-03-11"^^xsd:date ;
    dcterms:source <http://data.europa.eu/eli/reg/2014/1299/2023-09-28> ;
    rdfs:comment "Maximum value of the gradient for stabling tracks expressed in millimetres per metre."@en ;
    rdfs:domain [ a owl:Class ;
            owl:unionOf [ a rdf:List ;
                    rdf:first onto:CommonCharacteristicsSubset ;
                    rdf:rest [ a rdf:List ;
                            rdf:first onto:Siding ;
                            rdf:rest () ] ] ] ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy onto: ;
    rdfs:range xsd:double ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf onto:sidingDataParameter ;
    ns1:term_status "stable" .

onto:gradientProfile a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "Gradient profile"@en ;
    onto:XMLName "ILL_GradProfile" ;
    onto:applicable "Y" ;
    onto:formatNote "in XML:  +/-NN.N (+/-NNNN.NNN)" ;
    onto:legalDeadline "In accordance with Implementing Decision 2014/880/EU and by 16 March 2019 at the latest"@en ;
    onto:rinfIndex "1.1.1.1.3.6" ;
    onto:shaclShapeValidationRule <http://data.europa.eu/949/shapes/GradientProfile> ;
    onto:tsiOPEAppendixD2Index "3.2.1",
        "3.2.2" ;
    onto:usedInRCCCalculations true ;
    dcterms:created "2020-08-24"^^xsd:date ;
    dcterms:modified "2021-09-10"^^xsd:date,
        "2024-09-19"^^xsd:date,
        "2025-02-28"^^xsd:date ;
    dcterms:source <http://data.europa.eu/eli/reg/2014/1299/2023-09-28> ;
    rdfs:comment "Sequence of gradient values and locations of change in gradient"@en ;
    rdfs:domain [ a owl:Class ;
            owl:unionOf [ a rdf:List ;
                    rdf:first onto:CommonCharacteristicsSubset ;
                    rdf:rest [ a rdf:List ;
                            rdf:first onto:RunningTrack ;
                            rdf:rest () ] ] ] ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy onto: ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string ;
    rdfs:seeAlso "INF TSI: 4.2.3.3" ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf onto:lineLayoutDataParameter ;
    ns1:term_status "stable" ;
    skos:scopeNote "Data on the values of gradient along a SoL is given as a chain of information:\\n\\nGradient (location) The first location corresponding to the start of the first value of the gradient is the centre point of start OP. If there are different values of the gradient, the parameter will be repeated. The last location will correspond to the point where the last value of the gradient starts. This value will be available until the centre point of the end OP. \\n\\nIf there is only one value for the gradient along the track, then the location is not required, only the +/-NN.N value is expected.\\n\\nGradient is expressed in mm/m; location is expressed in km of the line.\\n\\nPositive gradient (uphill) is marked with \"+\" and negative gradient (downhill) is marked by \"-\".\\n\\nThe sequence shall follow the increasing kilometres of the line, and this does not take into consideration the running direction of the specific track. This will make the profile easier to read.\\n\\nChanges in gradient shall be registered only as far as necessary for train running calculations (minimum length of constant gradient shall be 500 m, the minimum change of gradient value shall be 0,5 mm/m).\\n\\nThe required precision for gradient value is 0,5 mm/m, the required precision of location of the points of change of gradient is 10 m. The points of change of gradient are the points of vertical intersection of each vertical curve."@en .

onto:gsmRAdditionalInfo a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "Additional information on network characteristics"@en ;
    onto:XMLName "CRG_AdditionalnetworkInfo" ;
    onto:applicable "Y/N/NYA" ;
    onto:dependencyNote "GSM-R must be installed for this parameter to be applicable"@en ;
    onto:legalDeadline "1 January 2021"@en,
        "12 months after publication of Article 7 Guide for OP tracks"@en ;
    onto:rinfIndex "1.1.1.3.3.3.1",
        "1.2.1.1.2.3.1" ;
    onto:shaclShapeValidationRule <http://data.europa.eu/949/shapes/GsmRAdditionalInfo>,
        <http://data.europa.eu/949/shapes/GsmRAdditionalInfoApplicability> ;
    dcterms:created "2021-08-08"^^xsd:date ;
    dcterms:modified "2021-09-12"^^xsd:date,
        "2024-04-18"^^xsd:date,
        "2024-09-19"^^xsd:date ;
    dcterms:relation onto:gprsForETCS ;
    rdfs:comment "Any additional information on network characteristics or corresponding document available from the IM and stored by the Agency, e.g.; interference level, leading to the recommendation of additional on-board protection."@en ;
    rdfs:domain [ a owl:Class ;
            owl:unionOf [ a rdf:List ;
                    rdf:first onto:CommonCharacteristicsSubset ;
                    rdf:rest [ a rdf:List ;
                            rdf:first onto:RunningTrack ;
                            rdf:rest () ] ] ] ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy onto: ;
    rdfs:range onto:Document ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf onto:tsiCompliantRadioObjParameter ;
    ns1:term_status "stable" ;
    skos:changeNote "Change from datatype property to object property in order to point to the class Document (reference document)"@en ;
    skos:scopeNote "Please use this field to indicate any additional information on the GSM-R network. \\n\\nThe value of this parameter should be either a reference to a file name or an external link to a document. \\nIf a file name is provided, the Infrastructure Manager (IM) must upload a document with the same file name using the \"Reference Documents Management\" functionality in the RINF application. The document must be in electronic format and available in two official EU languages. In this case, the parameter value must be repeated for each document. \\nIf an external link is provided, the IM must ensure that the document is available at the provided link."@en .

onto:gsmRNoCoverage a owl:DatatypeProperty,
        owl:FunctionalProperty ;
    rdfs:label "No GSMR coverage"@en ;
    onto:XMLName "CRG_GSMRNoCoverage" ;
    onto:applicable "Y/N/NYA" ;
    onto:dependencyNote "GSM-R (parameter 1.1.1.3.3.1) must be installed for this parameter to be applicable."@en ;
    onto:legalDeadline "1 January 2021"@en,
        "12 months after publication of Article 7 Guide for OP tracks"@en ;
    onto:rinfIndex "1.1.1.3.3.8",
        "1.2.1.1.2.8" ;
    onto:shaclShapeValidationRule <http://data.europa.eu/949/shapes/GsmRNoCoverage>,
        <http://data.europa.eu/949/shapes/GsmRNoCoverageApplicability> ;
    dcterms:created "2021-08-09"^^xsd:date ;
    dcterms:modified "2021-09-12"^^xsd:date,
        "2024-09-19"^^xsd:date,
        "2025-03-04"^^xsd:date ;
    rdfs:comment "Indication if there is no GSMR coverage"@en ;
    rdfs:domain [ a owl:Class ;
            owl:unionOf [ a rdf:List ;
                    rdf:first onto:CommonCharacteristicsSubset ;
                    rdf:rest [ a rdf:List ;
                            rdf:first onto:RunningTrack ;
                            rdf:rest () ] ] ] ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy onto: ;
    rdfs:range xsd:boolean ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf onto:tsiCompliantRadioDataParameter ;
    ns1:term_status "stable" ;
    skos:scopeNote "If GSM-R is not installed, this parameter should not be used.\\nThis parameter is mainly to capture the case of Radio Hole functionality (lack of GSM-R coverage), that is foreseen in the ETCS specifications as packet 68. \\nAnother possible use is the declaration of a temporary situation where, although the area is in principle covered by GSM-R, there is a long-term outage or a project for replacement of the radio (i.e. a section that will not be covered with GSM-R for half a year or longer)."@en .

onto:gsmROptionalFunctions a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "Optional GSM-R functions"@en ;
    onto:XMLName "CRG_OptionalFunctions" ;
    onto:applicable "Y/N/NYA" ;
    onto:dependencyNote "GSM-R (parameter 1.1.1.3.3.1) must be installed for this parameter to be applicable"@en ;
    onto:inSkosConceptScheme <http://data.europa.eu/949/concepts/gsmr-optional-functions/OptionalFunctions> ;
    onto:legalDeadline "12 months after publication of Article 7 Guide for OP tracks"@en,
        "In accordance with Implementing Decision 2014/880/EU and by 16 March 2019 at the latest"@en ;
    onto:rinfIndex "1.1.1.3.3.3",
        "1.2.1.1.2.3" ;
    onto:shaclShapeValidationRule <http://data.europa.eu/949/shapes/GsmROptionalFunctions>,
        <http://data.europa.eu/949/shapes/GsmROptionalFunctionsApplicability>,
        <http://data.europa.eu/949/shapes/GsmROptionalFunctionsSKOS> ;
    dcterms:created "2021-08-08"^^xsd:date ;
    dcterms:modified "2021-09-12"^^xsd:date,
        "2024-04-18"^^xsd:date ;
    rdfs:comment "Use of optional GSM-R functions which might improve operation on the line. They are for information only and not for network access criteria."@en ;
    rdfs:domain [ a owl:Class ;
            owl:unionOf [ a rdf:List ;
                    rdf:first onto:CommonCharacteristicsSubset ;
                    rdf:rest [ a rdf:List ;
                            rdf:first onto:RunningTrack ;
                            rdf:rest () ] ] ] ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy onto: ;
    rdfs:range skos:Concept ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf onto:tsiCompliantRadioObjParameter ;
    ns1:term_status "stable" ;
    skos:scopeNote "(*1) These inputs refer to the expected behaviour by the network, i.e. if there is any area or point where an automatic selection of network should be done or if there is any location where balises to instruct a change of radio network have been installed. \\nIn order to be able to attend to these indications (automatic network, network change by balise) some configuration is needed in the mobile.\\nIn case there is a balise used to announce the change of the network, or if there are locations where the network selection is planned by the IM to be done automatically (and not manually, as stated in the requirements). It should be considered as an item that is related to the design of the infrastructure.\\n\\n(*2) the possibility to dial 112 is something specific to the network that should be communicated to the vehicles accessing it.\\n\\n(*3) the use of broadcast calls is something specific to the network that has to be configured in it.\\n\\n(*4) it is something specific to the network that has to be configured in it if the service is provided.\\n\\n(*5) it is something specific to the network that has to be configured in it if the service is provided; something may need to be configured on the network but also in the mobile subscriber data if it wants to use the service. What is requested here is the information of the network capability.\\n\\n(*6) if they are configured on the network. Please indicate which in the \"Other information\" box.\\n\\n(*7) To be selected if other data applications, different from ETCS L2, can be used within the network - \\n\\n(*8) if it is configured on the network.\\n \"GSM-R Shunting used\" in order to make public if the GSM-R is used in the network for shunting activities. \\n\\n(*9) Please specify in the \"Other information\" box for which services /applications are they planned and which are the frequencies in use.\\n\\n(*11) Please use this field to indicate any additional information on network characteristics, e.g.; interference level, leading to the need of additional on-board protection;\\n"@en .

