onto:hasSevereWeatherConditions a owl:DatatypeProperty,
        owl:FunctionalProperty ;
    rdfs:label "Existence of severe climatic conditions"@en ;
    onto:XMLName "IPP_SevereClimateCon" ;
    onto:applicable "Y/N" ;
    onto:legalDeadline "In accordance with Implementing Decision 2014/880/EU and by 16 March 2019 at the latest"@en ;
    onto:rinfIndex "1.1.1.1.2.8" ;
    onto:shaclShapeValidationRule <http://data.europa.eu/949/shapes/HasSevereWeatherConditions> ;
    onto:usedInRCCCalculations true ;
    dcterms:created "2020-08-24"^^xsd:date ;
    dcterms:modified "2021-09-10"^^xsd:date,
        "2024-09-19"^^xsd:date ;
    dcterms:source <http://data.europa.eu/eli/reg/2014/1302/2023-09-28> ;
    rdfs:comment "Climatic conditions on the line are severe according to European standard."@en ;
    rdfs:domain [ a owl:Class ;
            owl:unionOf [ a rdf:List ;
                    rdf:first onto:CommonCharacteristicsSubset ;
                    rdf:rest [ a rdf:List ;
                            rdf:first onto:RunningTrack ;
                            rdf:rest () ] ] ] ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy onto: ;
    rdfs:range xsd:boolean ;
    rdfs:seeAlso "EN 50125-1 (2014): 4.7\\nLOC&PAS TSI:4.2.6.1.2" ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf onto:performanceDataParameter ;
    ns1:term_status "stable" ;
    skos:scopeNote "Value 'true' shall be selected in case there are possible severe climatic conditions to be expected, i.e. a significant amount of snow or ice is to be expected during winter and vehicle should be designed accordingly to be able to run in such conditions. (compliance to 4.2.6.1.2(3),(4) of TSI Loc&Pas required). 'False' to be selected otherwise.\\n\\nNominal and severe conditions are defined at TSI Loc&Pas level, section 4.2.6.1.2, which requires that the applicant declares to which snow conditions a vehicle complies with : either \"nominal\" or \"severe\" conditions. This technical aspect is reflected in the parameter 4.3.3 \"Snow, ice and hail conditions\" of ERATV , which will provide the two possible values:\\n- Nominal conditions correspond to compliance with clause 4.7 of EN 50125 as referred in the §4.2.6.1.2 (1) of TSI Loc&Pas.\\nTo be noted: It is not required to precise the categorisation S1, S2 or S3 as mentioned in the EN 50125.\\n- Severe conditions correspond to compliance with §4.2.6.1.2 (3) and (4) : the applicant designs and tests its vehicle according to the different scenarios mentioned in the TSI §4.2.6.1.2 (3) (snowdrift, powder snow, temperature gradient, etc.) and set the related provisions to achieve this as required by §4.2.6.1.2 (4) (obstacle deflector of sufficient size, effect of ice and snow on running gear and brake function, etc.)."@en .

