onto:lineCategory a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "Category of line"@en ;
    onto:XMLName "IPP_LineCat" ;
    onto:applicable "Y/N" ;
    onto:inSkosConceptScheme <http://data.europa.eu/949/concepts/line-category/LineCategories> ;
    onto:legalDeadline "In accordance with Implementing Decision 2014/880/EU and by 16 March 2019 at the latest"@en ;
    onto:rinfIndex "1.1.1.1.2.2",
        "1.2.1.0.2.2" ;
    onto:shaclShapeValidationRule <http://data.europa.eu/949/shapes/LineCategory>,
        <http://data.europa.eu/949/shapes/LineCategorySKOS> ;
    dcterms:created "2021-08-02"^^xsd:date ;
    dcterms:modified "2024-01-08"^^xsd:date,
        "2024-09-19"^^xsd:date ;
    dcterms:source <http://data.europa.eu/eli/reg/2014/1299/2023-09-28> ;
    rdfs:comment "Classification of a line according to the TSI INF"@en ;
    rdfs:domain [ a owl:Class ;
            owl:unionOf [ a rdf:List ;
                    rdf:first onto:CommonCharacteristicsSubset ;
                    rdf:rest [ a rdf:List ;
                            rdf:first onto:RunningTrack ;
                            rdf:rest () ] ] ] ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy onto: ;
    rdfs:range skos:Concept ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf onto:performanceObjParameter ;
    ns1:term_status "stable" ;
    skos:example "If a line is operated by passenger trains with speed of 250 km/h, local commuter trains with speed of 120 km/h and heavy freight trains in the night, then the best combination of traffic codes seems to be P2, P5 and F1. \\nThen, the TSI category of line for this case would simply be P2-P5-F1." ;
    skos:scopeNote "INF TSI (4.2.1) classifies lines based on the type of traffic (traffic code).\\n\\nTSI categories of line shall be used for the classification of existing lines to define a target system so that the relevant performance parameters will be met.\\n\\nThe TSI category of line is a combination of traffic codes. For lines where only one type of traffic is carried (for example a freight only line), a single code can be used to describe the requirements; where mixed traffic runs the category will be described by one or more codes for passenger and freight in case of two types of traffic. Then the parameter is repeated if relevant. The combined traffic codes describe the envelope within which the desired mix of traffic can be accommodated.\\n\\nTechnical scope of the INF TSI includes all the networks (TEN and off-TEN) for nominal track gauges 1435, 1520, 1524, 1600 and 1668 mm.\\nIt is not applicable when track is not included in technical scope of the TSI. \\nWhen more than one value of the parameter has to be published, then parameter has to be repeated as many times as many values of the parameter will be published."@en .

